# .ragignore — what the index should skip. gitignore syntax; one pattern per line.
# Lives at .rag/.ragignore. Applied on top of the built-in skip list and, when
# corpus.use_gitignore is true, each source's .gitignore.
#
# ALREADY BUILT IN, do not repeat here: any file or directory whose name starts with
# '.' or '_' is never indexed, at any depth. In this vault that already covers
# .obsidian/, .git/, .trash/, .tmp/, .wiki-index/, .DS_Store and _utils/.
#
# After editing, run:  rag plan     (see what changes)  then  rag update

# --- not notes, per the vault's own convention ------------------------------
# index.md lines 27-28 state: "Not notes, never indexed: _utils/ (MCP servers),
# Dev/LLM/ (code sandbox), Dev/languages/Python/*.py|.ipynb, .tmp/, .obsidian/,
# .wiki-index/". _utils/ and the dot-folders are already covered by the built-in
# private-name rule; these two are not, so they are declared here.
Dev/LLM/
Dev/languages/Python/*.py
Dev/languages/Python/*.ipynb

# Named like a credential. Excluded on the name alone — it has not been opened.
Dev/languages/Python/key.txt

# --- Excalidraw drawings ----------------------------------------------------
# These .md files are an Obsidian plugin wrapper around compressed drawing JSON.
# The prose in them is a handful of disconnected canvas labels ("like using PCA"),
# wrapped around a large base64 payload — it retrieves badly and dilutes real notes.
# Delete these three lines if you want the canvas text labels searchable.
Excalidraw/
*.excalidraw.md
*.excalidrawlib

# --- media ------------------------------------------------------------------
# No text extractor exists for these; listed so `rag plan` reports them as an
# intentional exclusion rather than an unhandled extension.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.svg
*.ico
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.mov
*.wav

# --- secrets: never index these ---------------------------------------------
# Defense in depth. `.env` is already covered by the built-in rule above, but a
# secret reaching an index leaks through search results forever, so both apply.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
credentials
secrets.*
